[0.034, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[93C\u001b[11B\u001b[1m[ 📌✓\r\u001b[91C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bf\u001b[5Gr commands, so c\u001b[22Gntrol ins\u001b[32Gructions (mov\u001b[47Gthe cursor, change color, clear\u001b[79Gthe screen)\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bhav\u001b[7G to b\u001b[13G embedde\u001b[23Gin-band alongside \u001b[42Ghe printable text.\u001b[61GT\u001b[63Ge ESC character (0x1B) marks\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe start of \u001b[17Guch an instruction, le\u001b[40Gting the terminal tell\u001b[63G\"do \u001b[68Ghis\" apart from \"display\r\u001b[1B  this.\"\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;183m◆ \u001b[38;5;109mNapped in 3s\r\u001b[6B\u001b[39m\u001b[1m[ 📌 ▸ ]\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246m Terminals use escape codes because they're a single text stream… \u001b[39m\u001b[1m[ ✕ ]\u001b[97G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246m[-]\r\u001b[96C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h\u001b[?2026l"]
